[gd_scene load_steps=12 format=3]

; ─────────────────────────────────────────────
; CAUSEWAY — THE GAMEPLAY LAYER, AS ITS OWN SCENE.
;
; The largest map in the repo and the end of the ladder. It has had no mission
; at all: before this, maps/causeway_level.tscn held an art instance, a nav
; region, ninety-eight tower lamps and one Marker3D. Nothing else.
;
; Same split as Georgetown and Polaris — the gameplay lives here, and
; tools/mission_ops.sh instances it — but for a different reason. This level is
; HAND-BUILT and is not regenerated, so the file is safe; what is not safe is
; putting two hundred nodes into a .tscn that also carries ninety-eight lights
; and then having to find anything in it. The split is for the reader here.
;
; ── THE GROUND, MEASURED ─────────────────────
; Everything below was walked with tools/probe_mission_anchors.gd against the
; baked navmesh in maps/causeway_level_nav.tres. The whole thing is one
; connected piece from the west bank to the top of the tower: 2,054 m of path.
;
;   WEST BANK      x -580..-320, y  1   ruins, a terrace row, a warehouse.
;                                       The end of the old highway.
;   THE CAUSEWAY   x -300..+324, y  5   thirteen 48 m spans, 16 m of deck with
;                                       a 1 m parapet each side and NOTHING
;                                       else on it. Two spans are shelled
;                                       (x -132 and x +108): the north half of
;                                       the deck is gone over 20 m and the lane
;                                       pinches to 7 m. Three more have settled.
;   THE GLACIS     x +324..+430, y  1   wire, teeth, T-walls, two sangars, two
;                                       sentry turrets, a checkpoint and two gun
;                                       emplacements, then 60 m of ramp up to
;                                       the gate.
;   THE FORT       x +430..+630, y 10   200 m square podium. Walls 8 m thick to
;                                       a walk at 14 and bastions at 18. ONE
;                                       opening: the 16 m gateway in the west
;                                       wall. The outworks (mortar pits, command
;                                       bunker, ammunition dump) are OUTSIDE it.
;   THE PIT        x +618..+558        24 m wide, 1 in 6, down from the yard to
;                                       the basement. On the far side of the
;                                       yard from the gate on purpose.
;   THE TOWER      y 0..138            TWENTY-FOUR data halls, 41 m square, 6 m
;                                       floor to floor, one 7 m ramp per floor
;                                       rotating round the four walls. Rack rows
;                                       with 5 m aisles, and a clear lane 7 m in
;                                       from every wall.
;
; TWO THINGS THE MEASUREMENT SETTLED that change the design:
;
;   1. THE OLD CARRIAGEWAY IS NOT A ROUTE. The seven piers at z = +30 bake as
;      isolated stubs — (-276, 1, 30), (12, 1, 30) and (108, 1, 30) all come
;      back UNREACHABLE. They are a silhouette beside the crossing, not a flank,
;      so nothing is posted on them and no route uses them.
;   2. THE CROWN IS NOT WALKABLE. Everything asked for above y = 138 snaps back
;      to 138, so the top data hall is the top of the map. The uplink and the
;      pad are both on it, at opposite ends of the hall — which is the last
;      41 m of the operation and is meant to be crossed under fire.
;
; ── WHAT THE OPERATION IS ────────────────────
; Three fights of completely different shapes, in a row, which is the reason
; this map is the finale rather than another town:
;
;   1. A KILOMETRE OF OPEN DECK. There is no cover on the causeway worth the
;      word, so this cannot be a long-range attrition fight or it is the thing
;      the map deck already ruled is not fun. It is built as THREE CLOSE-RANGE
;      POCKETS instead — the two shelled spans and the midpoint — held by
;      shotguns, chasers and hoppers who are already in the 7 m pinch when you
;      get there. Nothing on the deck is a marksman. The long guns are in the
;      fort where they belong and only reach the last third.
;   2. A FORTRESS WITH ONE DOOR. Dug-in armour on a glacis, then a gateway, then
;      a 200 m yard overlooked from a wall walk on all four sides.
;   3. AN INTERIOR, TWENTY-FOUR FLOORS OF IT. The one real interior in the
;      project. Every floor is a 41 m room with one way in and one way on, and
;      the upper halls are held back as reserves so the body count rises as you
;      climb instead of all of it being awake from the basement.
; ─────────────────────────────────────────────

