; ── THE TOWER. One post per floor, all twenty-four. ──
;
; WHICH SIDE OF THE HALL EACH ONE IS ON IS NOT ARBITRARY. The ramp up from
; floor n sits against one of the four inside walls and rotates with n % 4, so
; the hole you come UP through on floor n is above the ramp from n-1:
;
;   n % 4 == 1  you arrive on the +z side   ->  post on -x, at x 513
;   n % 4 == 2  you arrive on the +x side   ->  post on -x, at x 513
;   n % 4 == 3  you arrive on the -z side   ->  post on +z, at z 17
;   n % 4 == 0  you arrive on the -x side   ->  post on +z, at z 17
;
; So the garrison is always across the room from the stairwell rather than
; standing on top of it, and every floor is entered the same way: through a
; hole, into a 41 m room, with the defence on the far side of it.
;
; x 513 and z 17 are both in the clear lane 7 m in from the wall. The rack rows
; run x 516.5..543.5 on a 7 m pitch, so the hall centre is racks and aisles and
; the perimeter is the only ground a squad can actually form up on.
;
; FLOOR 0 is the exception twice over: it is the hall you come in to through
; the portal in the +x face, and block_fortress leaves it empty of racks on
; purpose so the fight has room to start. Both of its posts are authored.
