; THE WALL WALK IS TWO RUNS, NOT A CIRCUIT. It is cut at the gatehouse in the
; west wall and again at the pit head in the east, so each half is an L from
; one bastion along a wall to the next and then down the east side as far as
; the gap. Authored as two routes rather than one loop: a single route spanning
; both halves would have the squad path down a ramp, across two hundred metres
; of yard and back up the far side on every lap, which is not a wall patrol.
